WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.185 --> 00:00:17.809
The day after the coronation, Miles stood outside the palace.

2
00:00:20.329 --> 00:00:23.630
He'd searched for Edward for two days but couldn't find the boy.

3
00:00:25.711 --> 00:00:30.132
So, Miles decided to seek help from his father's friend who worked at the palace.

4
00:00:31.516 --> 00:00:33.717
Just then Marlow came through the gate.

5
00:00:33.737 --> 00:00:35.798
"Do you work at the palace?"

6
00:00:36.258 --> 00:00:36.999
Miles asked.

7
00:00:37.019 --> 00:00:39.180
"Do you know Sir Marlow?"

8
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.601
"That's my father!"

9
00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:42.941
Marlow exclaimed.

10
00:00:42.961 --> 00:00:49.304
"Tell him that Miles Hendon, son of Sir Richard Hendon, urgently needs to see him."

11
00:00:49.324 --> 00:00:55.067
"Unfortunately, my father died last year," Marlow explained.

12
00:00:55.087 --> 00:00:57.768
"But I know someone who can help you."

13
00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:03.603
Marlow led Miles into the palace courtyard and told him to wait.

14
00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:09.368
Shaking his head in disbelief, Marlow hurried into the palace.

15
00:01:10.749 --> 00:01:12.891
"The king sent me to look for his friend.

16
00:01:13.912 --> 00:01:16.254
And there he was—right outside!"

17
00:01:17.895 --> 00:01:20.838
As Miles leaned against a wall, a guard approached him.

18
00:01:20.858 --> 00:01:23.820
"What are you doing here?"

19
00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:24.921
the guard said.

20
00:01:24.941 --> 00:01:28.264
"We can't have loafers around the palace!"

21
00:01:29.716 --> 00:01:34.119
Suddenly Miles remembered Edward's note in his pocket and handed it to the guard.

22
00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:38.342
He'd forgotten about it amid all the trouble with Hugh.

23
00:01:38.362 --> 00:01:41.844
"This ought to help me," Miles thought.

24
00:01:43.305 --> 00:01:45.847
But the guard's face clouded over as he read the note.

25
00:01:45.867 --> 00:01:49.510
"Not another fellow claiming to be the king!

26
00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.892
I'm arresting you for—" "For nothing!"

27
00:01:53.993 --> 00:01:56.134
Marlow hurried over to the guard and stopped him.

28
00:01:57.255 --> 00:02:02.003
Then he turned to Miles, bowed respectfully, and said, "Please come with me, sir."

29
00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:11.370
Miles followed Marlow into a room where a line of people stood waiting to speak to the king.

30
00:02:12.631 --> 00:02:14.893
When the king looked up, Miles gasped.

31
00:02:14.913 --> 00:02:19.017
"Is that my young friend?"

32
00:02:20.218 --> 00:02:21.258
Miles rubbed his eyes.

33
00:02:21.278 --> 00:02:23.941
"There's only one way to be sure."

34
00:02:25.842 --> 00:02:27.784
Miles went over to a chair and sat down.

35
00:02:29.064 --> 00:02:30.785
Instantly a guard was at his side.

36
00:02:30.805 --> 00:02:33.925
"You can't just come in here and sit down!"

37
00:02:34.325 --> 00:02:35.426
the guard said loudly.

38
00:02:35.446 --> 00:02:39.287
The king laughed.

39
00:02:40.207 --> 00:02:41.207
"Oh yes, he can.

40
00:02:42.588 --> 00:02:47.529
This is Sir Miles, my trusty companion, and he's allowed to sit whenever I'm sitting.

41
00:02:48.669 --> 00:02:50.690
Hello, Miles, how are you today?"

42
00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:56.031
"Very well, Your Majesty, though I'm surprised to see you here."

43
00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:03.743
On the outside Miles was laughing but inside he was embarrassed.

44
00:03:03.763 --> 00:03:10.348
"I can't believe I bragged to King Edward that we have seventy rooms and thirty servants at Hendon

45
00:03:10.388 --> 00:03:14.050
Hall! That's nothing compared to what he's used to."

46
00:03:16.012 --> 00:03:19.974
Struggling to believe Edward was really the king, Miles stared at the boy.

47
00:03:19.994 --> 00:03:23.537
"This is my pauper?

48
00:03:24.658 --> 00:03:26.739
This is the boy I vowed to protect?"

49
00:03:27.159 --> 00:03:27.820
Miles thought.

50
00:03:29.304 --> 00:03:31.805
"He has guards and a whole army to protect him!"

51
00:03:34.445 --> 00:03:36.646
Miles stepped forward and bowed to the king.

52
00:03:39.087 --> 00:03:42.748
Then he stood aside while Edward scanned the people waiting to speak to him.

53
00:03:44.168 --> 00:03:47.849
The king spotted some people he recognized and beckoned them forward.

54
00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:54.191
Miles drew his breath in sharply as Hugh and Edith approached the king.

55
00:03:56.111 --> 00:03:59.369
When Hugh asked to be made an earl, Edward's face hardened.

56
00:03:59.389 --> 00:04:01.971
"You don't deserve the honor.

57
00:04:03.072 --> 00:04:08.055
Miles and I spent time in jail, thanks to you, and Miles spent time in the stocks."

58
00:04:09.856 --> 00:04:10.857
Edward called a guard.

59
00:04:10.877 --> 00:04:13.979
"Arrest this man.

60
00:04:17.602 --> 00:04:20.204
I strip him of his stolen title and property."

61
00:04:20.224 --> 00:04:22.765
"I didn't know you were the king!"

62
00:04:22.785 --> 00:04:28.409
Hugh protested as he was led away, but Edward was no longer paying attention.

63
00:04:28.429 --> 00:04:35.273
"Now, Lady Edith, you can tell me the truth," King Edward said kindly.

64
00:04:35.293 --> 00:04:39.035
"Did you recognize Miles at Hendon Hall?"

65
00:04:41.356 --> 00:04:44.398
Miles held his breath, waiting for Edith's response.

66
00:04:44.418 --> 00:04:47.479
"Yes," she said quietly.

67
00:04:47.499 --> 00:04:52.402
"My husband told me to lie and threatened to punish me if I didn't.

68
00:04:53.483 --> 00:04:55.684
When I said I didn't care, he threatened to hurt Miles."

69
00:04:57.836 --> 00:05:00.277
"My Edith was trying to protect me!"

70
00:05:00.737 --> 00:05:01.858
Miles said fondly.

71
00:05:01.878 --> 00:05:06.580
"I banish Hugh from my kingdom forever!"

72
00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:07.840
Edward declared.

73
00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:14.003
"Next!" Tom stepped forward and bowed to the king.

74
00:05:14.023 --> 00:05:16.424
"Tom Canty!"

75
00:05:17.524 --> 00:05:18.325
Edward smiled.

76
00:05:18.345 --> 00:05:24.147
"As a reward for taking care of my kingdom, you shall become head of the home for poor,

77
00:05:24.507 --> 00:05:25.528
abandoned children.

78
00:05:27.436 --> 00:05:29.937
You're welcome to live there with your mother and sister.

79
00:05:31.278 --> 00:05:32.219
Have you found them again?"

80
00:05:32.239 --> 00:05:39.643
"Yes, Your Majesty, and I apologized to my mother for pretending not to know her," Tom said.

81
00:05:39.663 --> 00:05:43.105
"I wasn't quite myself, as you know, sir."

82
00:05:44.826 --> 00:05:45.666
"I understand."

83
00:05:46.887 --> 00:05:48.127
King Edward smiled.

84
00:05:49.688 --> 00:05:55.191
That day Edward wanted to arrest John Canty for cruelty to his family, but no one could find

85
00:05:55.251 --> 00:06:04.464
him. In the years that followed, Hugh died in prison, which freed Edith to marry Miles.

86
00:06:06.366 --> 00:06:10.009
Tom became good friends with the king and was often seen at court.

87
00:06:15.673 --> 00:06:22.499
As for King Edward himself Whenever someone complained that he was too kind to the poor, he told

88
00:06:22.539 --> 00:06:23.019
a story.

89
00:06:24.621 --> 00:06:28.384
It was the tale of how he, a prince, had become a pauper.

90
00:06:29.813 --> 00:06:34.535
"And that," he always said, "has made me a better king!"
